{
	title: 'Session states: pause only on purpose',
	spec: 'Give every session one explicit state that the host derives from history plus its own memory, and put it in snapshots so every client shows the same thing. The rules and the state list are in states.md (decisions made with the user, not suggestions). Core: only the user pauses work (Escape pauses that session; Ctrl-C pauses everything only when no other Hal process can carry on). A restart (Ctrl-R) or a host that dies while another process remains must continue every running turn as if nothing happened. Implement the pure transition function with table tests, the durable paused marker, the automatic continuation on a new host, and snapshot status; replace task ah behaviour (turns are left interrupted) accordingly. Retries, blocked reasons, steering and amend are separate tasks that extend this machine; leave their states defined but unimplemented.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"The machine is src/common/states.ts: states.step(state, event) returns the next state or a refusal string (sent back as `rejected`). host.transition() is the only writer of in-memory state and broadcasts a `state` event when it changes; host.stateOf() falls back to states.fromHistory(). Extend step() and its table test for new states; don't set host.state.states by hand.",
		'Durable records: a turn end with status `paused` (plus `pauseReason` when Hal, not the user, paused it) and a `continue` record. A turn with no end record is unfinished and reads as running; host.recover() (called from main.becomeHost after server.serve) continues every unfinished session by appending `continue`. `cancelled` and `interrupted` survive only in old histories and read as paused.',
		"replay.toMessages turns a `continue` into: error results for unanswered calls ('may or may not have run' after a pause or host death), then the continue note if the last message was the assistant's. After tool results or a failed request nothing is added, so continue after an error resends the same request (tf builds retrying on this).",
		'Loop guard: states.recoveries() counts `continue` records at the end of history with only assistant output between; recover() pauses with a reason at states.maxRecoveries() (5). Partial output is not progress, tool results or a turn end are. User continues are separated by paused turn ends, so they never trip it.',
		'Ctrl-C: terminal.onQuit (sync, try-wrapped) → host.quitting(last), where last = no peer on the host socket (server.state.sockets). The exit handler then runs history.stop(pause): flush output so far, and write a paused end only for the last process. Ctrl-R, SIGTERM and SIGKILL write no end; the next host continues. Usage of the cut-off round is lost in that case (turn_end carries usage).',
		'Clients never decide from transcript.live any more: states.enter()/states.escape() map Enter/Escape to submit, continue or pause from Transcript.state, for terminal and web alike. Escape must pause a turn that is running on disk but not in this host (another host still recovering): host.stop() writes the paused end directly, and transcript.fold appends a turn-end even with no live turn.',
		"For 2r (steering): step() refuses submit while busy; accept it there and keep the inbox outside the state. For tf (retries): nothing produces `retrying` yet; add a retry event into it (step already takes retrying to running on `request`, and to paused on Escape). For wb (amend): pause then decide from history since the last prompt. For nn (replay): continue records and paused ends are display-silent except the [paused] item.",
		'Test for recovery by stopping the process in memory: history.stop(false) then host.reset() + sessions.closeAll() + history.state.running.clear(), then await host.recover(). The e2e tests cover Ctrl-C with and without a peer and Ctrl-R mid-turn.'
	],
	needs: ['1r'],
	foldInto: ['6', 'ne', 'ah']
}
